# Why: Upload/download/delete operations and presigned URL generation must
#      consult the BizRethink `BizrethinkInstanceStorageConfig` singleton
#      row (S3 endpoint, bucket, region, access keys, CloudFront/Cloudflare
#      distribution domain + key) BEFORE falling back to env vars. This
#      lets operators change storage configuration via the admin UI
#      (/admin/instance-storage) without a Coolify redeploy + container
#      restart.
#
#      Two integration points in this file:
#
#        1. `resolveStorageSettings()` — new helper (lines 144-176) that
#           dynamically imports `getInstanceStorageConfig()` from
#           @bizrethink/customizations and returns a resolved
#           `{ provider, endpoint, region, bucket, accessKeyId, ...}`
#           object with DB-first + env-fallback semantics. Dynamic import
#           is used to avoid a circular dependency between @documenso/lib
#           and @bizrethink/customizations (the latter depends on prisma
#           which depends back into lib).
#
#        2. `getPresignGetUrl()` — call site that uses `resolveStorageSettings()`
#           to read the distribution settings (CloudFront domain + signing
#           key) when constructing the presigned download URL (lines 72-84).
#
#      The companion module `packages/bizrethink/server-only/instance-storage-
#      config.ts` is a new file (outside upstream's tree, no patch needed).
#      It implements: prisma read of the singleton row, in-process cache
#      with 60s TTL, env-fallback merging, and `invalidateInstanceStorage-
#      Config()` for the admin UI's "save" handler to call.
#
# Why-not-additive: `getS3Client()` and `getPresignGetUrl()` are upstream
#      exports that downstream code (the UI, webhooks, seal job's
#      `putPdfFileServerSide()`) calls directly. There's no extension
#      point or DI to inject our resolver. Inline patch is the only path.
#
# Upstream-merge-fragility: MEDIUM.
#   - The integration site in `getPresignGetUrl()` (~line 73) anchors on
#     the function signature and the `distribution = ...` resolution
#     block. Upstream rarely touches this file (last commit was the
#     biome lint sweep, 8671f269e, 2026-05-15).
#   - The `resolveStorageSettings()` helper at the bottom of the file
#     is purely additive — no anchor risk.
#   - If upstream changes the S3 client interface or distribution
#     types (e.g., adds R2 support natively), we'd need to update the
#     `ResolvedStorageSettings` type to match.
#
# Caveat — DB unavailable behavior: If the DB read for
#      `BizrethinkInstanceStorageConfig` throws (Postgres down, network
#      flap), `resolveStorageSettings()` catches the error and falls
#      back to env-only values. This means a temporarily-bad DB does
#      NOT break uploads — but a permanently-misconfigured DB row WILL
#      override correct env values silently. Recommend validating the
#      DB row via "Test Connection" button in admin UI before saving.
#
# Status: PATCHIFIED 2026-05-25 from inline `// MODIFIED for BizRethink
#         (overlay 013)` markers that had been live since the admin UI
#         for storage config shipped. Backfilling discipline before
